Bilkul bhai 👍

Ye topics tumhe Playwright user se Framework Developer mindset ki taraf le jaate hain. SDET interviews mein bahut value rakhte hain.

1. Logger

Abhi tum:

TypeScript
console.log(responseBody);
console.log(token);

kar rahe ho.

Professional framework:

TypeScript
Logger.info("Booking Created");
Logger.error("Token Generation Failed");

Example:

TypeScript
export class Logger {
static info(message: string) {
console.log(`[INFO] ${message}`);
}
 
static error(message: string) {
console.log(`[ERROR] ${message}`);
}
}

Usage:

TypeScript
Logger.info("Create booking started");

Output:

Plain Text
[INFO] Create booking started
2. Retry Mechanism

Kabhi API temporary fail hoti hai:

Plain Text
500 Internal Server Error
502 Bad Gateway
503 Service Unavailable

Test immediately fail karne ke bajaye retry kar sakta hai.

Example:

TypeScript
export async function retryApi(
apiCall: () => Promise<any>,
retries = 3
) {
for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
const response = await apiCall();
 
if (response.ok()) {
return response;
}
}
 
throw new Error("API Failed");
}

Usage:

TypeScript
const response = await retryApi(
() => bookingAPI.getBooking(1)
);
3. Utility Classes

Abhi agar date generate karni hai:

TypeScript
const date = "2026-11-30";

Har jagah same code.

Utility class:

TypeScript
export class DateUtil {
 
static getTodayDate() {
return new Date()
.toISOString()
.split("T")[0];
}
 
}

Usage:

TypeScript
DateUtil.getTodayDate();

Another example:

TypeScript
export class RandomUtil {
 
static getRandomNumber() {
return Math.floor(Math.random() * 1000);
}
 
}
4. Response Validator ⭐

Abhi:

TypeScript
expect(response.status()).toBe(200);
expect(body.firstname)
.toBe("Sameer");

Har test mein repeat.

Create validator:

TypeScript
export class ResponseValidator {
 
static validateStatus(
response: any,
expectedStatus: number
) {
expect(response.status())
.toBe(expectedStatus);
}
 
}

Usage:

TypeScript
ResponseValidator
.validateStatus(response, 200);
 

Advanced:

TypeScript
ResponseValidator
.validateStatus(response, 201);
 
ResponseValidator
.validateJsonSchema(body, schema);
5. Generic Base API ⭐⭐⭐

Ye sabse important hai.

Abhi shayad:

TypeScript
BookingAPI.ts
TokenAPI.ts
UserAPI.ts

har file mein:

TypeScript
request.get()
request.post()
request.put()

repeat hoga.

Create:

TypeScript
export class BaseAPI {
 
constructor(
protected request: APIRequestContext
) {}
 
async get(url: string) {
return await this.request.get(url);
}
 
async post(
url: string,
payload: any
) {
return await this.request.post(url,{
data: payload
});
}
}

BookingAPI:

TypeScript
export class BookingAPI extends BaseAPI {
 
async getBooking(id:number) {
return this.get(`/booking/${id}`);
}
 
}

Ab duplicate code kam ho jayega.

Real SDET Structure
Plain Text
src
 
├── api
│ ├── BaseAPI.ts
│ ├── BookingAPI.ts
│ └── TokenAPI.ts
 
├── utils
│ ├── Logger.ts
│ ├── DateUtil.ts
│ └── RandomUtil.ts
 
├── validators
│ ├── ResponseValidator.ts
│ └── SchemaValidator.ts
 
├── data
│ └── TestData.ts
 
└── tests
Mere hisab se next order
✅ Base API
✅ Response Validator
✅ Logger
✅ Utility Classes
✅ Retry Mechanism

Tum already Factory Pattern aur API Framework touch kar chuke ho, isliye BaseAPI + ResponseValidator next logical step hai. Ye interview mein bhi strong SDET-level discussion point banega. 🚀